<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 3 May, from 1469 to 1937.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World Press Freedom Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Proclaimed by the UN General Assembly in 1993 on the anniversary of the Windhoek Declaration, World Press Freedom Day affirms that a free press is essential to democracy and evaluates the state of press freedom worldwide.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/niccolo-machiavelli" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niccolo-machiavelli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1469">1469 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">557 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Niccolò Machiavelli is born in Florence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niccolo-machiavelli">Machiavelli</a>, diplomat of the Florentine republic and author of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-prince">The Prince</a>, was born. His unsentimental analysis of power made him a founder of modern political thought.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1494">1494 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">532 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sights Jamaica on his second voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> called Xaymaca, and named it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>. The island remained under Spanish rule until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> captured it in 1655.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1660">1660 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">366 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Oliva makes peace between Sweden and Poland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Signed near Danzig, the treaty ended the war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>'s king renounced his claim to the Swedish throne and recognised Swedish rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Poland-Lithuania adopts the Constitution of 3 May</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a> passed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s first modern codified national constitution, strengthening the monarchy and ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberum-veto">liberum veto</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> responded with war and the second partition.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1814">1814 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon arrives off Elba to begin his exile</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">HMS Undaunted brought the deposed emperor to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portoferraio">Portoferraio</a>, where he landed the next morning to rule his tiny island principality. He escaped in February 1815.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1921">1921 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">105 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Northern Ireland comes into being</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Government of Ireland Act took effect, partitioning Ireland and creating Northern Ireland from six north-eastern counties with its own parliament. Partition remains in place today.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1937">1937 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Margaret Mitchell wins the Pulitzer for Gone with the Wind</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Margaret Mitchell's novel of the Civil War and Reconstruction won the Pulitzer Prize for Fiction. A huge bestseller, it was filmed in 1939, though its portrayal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> is now widely criticised.</p></div></li></ol>
